commit 818cf3646baca7218d7b15e7ef2e6ca7dd984f59
Author:     Jakub Skokan <jakub.skokan@havefun.cz>
AuthorDate: Thu Oct 8 10:34:21 2026 +0200
Commit:     Jakub Skokan <jakub.skokan@havefun.cz>
CommitDate: Thu Oct 8 10:34:21 2026 +0200

    webui: expose network availability and inventory
    
    Add confirmed administrator availability controls and keep disabled owned
    addresses visible without detached assignment actions. Enabled selectors
    follow advertised API capabilities and remain compatible with older APIs.
    
    Group network identity, properties, IP usage and actions in four columns.
    Use authoritative available and owned-unassigned counts with descriptions
    of ownership, interface assignment and capacity. Missing statistics remain
    unknown. Shade disabled routed-IP rows and explain them at the network
    address, preserving existing service links and stale-form guards.

commit adb6bb9cb24e0cf833fff6a9de40b87588cc13cf
Author:     Jakub Skokan <jakub.skokan@havefun.cz>
AuthorDate: Thu Oct 8 10:30:57 2026 +0200
Commit:     Jakub Skokan <jakub.skokan@havefun.cz>
CommitDate: Thu Oct 8 10:30:57 2026 +0200

    api: expose authoritative network inventory counts
    
    Count registered allocations available to users using the shared reservation
    scope, and report owned allocations without an interface assignment even in
    reserved or disabled inventory. These admin-only read-only fields distinguish
    available inventory from theoretical capacity and overlapping ownership totals.
    
    The output fields are additive and require no schema migration.

commit 5d5527a67315c18b595345aa6996d7724c1ed071
Author:     Jakub Skokan <jakub.skokan@havefun.cz>
AuthorDate: Wed Oct 7 00:07:08 2026 +0200
Commit:     Jakub Skokan <jakub.skokan@havefun.cz>
CommitDate: Wed Oct 7 02:17:35 2026 +0200

    api: restrict non-admin network and IP lists
    
    Disabled inventory is unavailable for new use and should be omitted from
    member lists. Retain owned and assigned addresses within existing
    permissions, and preserve direct Show and association access. Apply the
    restriction before counts and pagination; admin inventory stays unchanged.

commit 70314e816099855b31b56ee42d3b887e2195566a
Author:     Jakub Skokan <jakub.skokan@havefun.cz>
AuthorDate: Tue Oct 6 15:10:41 2026 +0200
Commit:     Jakub Skokan <jakub.skokan@havefun.cz>
CommitDate: Wed Oct 7 02:17:34 2026 +0200

    webui: expose network availability and enabled address selectors
    
    Show enabled state in network and owned-address inventory. Add a confirmed
    administrator POST form and exclude disabled pools from available selectors
    when the API advertises support. Keep old API requests compatible.
    
    Detached owned addresses in disabled networks remain visible with assignment
    controls unavailable, including stale assignment forms. Preserve controls for
    existing service and cover confirmation, CSRF and selector behavior.

commit fc4f01a025e373ba5c85a7e78ea8b61ac1e1dc1f
Author:     Jakub Skokan <jakub.skokan@havefun.cz>
AuthorDate: Tue Oct 6 15:09:44 2026 +0200
Commit:     Jakub Skokan <jakub.skokan@havefun.cz>
CommitDate: Tue Oct 6 16:51:37 2026 +0200

    api: add network availability admission controls
    
    Allow administrators to disable new use of a network without interrupting
    existing assigned addresses. Count available public IPv4 allocation rows
    only in enabled pools and expose optional availability metadata and filters.
    
    Capture each operation's source and destination networks before reserving IP
    rows, retaining that set through included allocations and retries. Recheck
    current address identity and eligibility after reservation while preserving
    trusted assigned-address continuity during migration, swap and restore.
    
    The additive enabled column defaults to true. Update all API writers before
    disabling a network; older writers do not enforce this policy.
